  "notes": "モテる comes from {持|も}てる (to be able to hold/have), meaning \"to be held in regard\" or \"to be in demand.\" Usually written in katakana to emphasize its slang nature.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is casual/colloquial language commonly used when discussing dating and popularity.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～にモテる: to be popular with (a group)\n- モテ{男|おとこ}/モテ{女|おんな}: a popular guy/girl\n- モテ{期|き}: a period when one is popular\n- モテたい: to want to be popular\n- {非|ひ}モテ: someone who isn't popular (slang)",
